Vite writes the marketing site here, and site/site.go embeds the result, so the
files themselves are not committed.

This file is committed, and must stay: //go:embed is a compile error when its
directory does not exist, so on a fresh clone its absence would break
`go build ./...`, `go vet ./...` and `go test ./...` — the entire local gate.

Run `make build` (or `npm --prefix site run build`) to populate it. A dist that
holds only this file compiles, starts, and serves a site with no stylesheet and
no scripts, so site.AssetsBuilt exists and cmd/drift warns on startup rather than
letting the deploy look healthy.
